aining the U3 snoRNA that is involved in processing of pre-18S rRNA	Subunit beta1 of the nascent polypeptide-associated complex (NAC) involved in protein targeting, associated with cytoplasmic ribosomes; enhances DNA binding of the Gal4p activator; homolog of human BTF3b	Integral membrane component of endoplasmic reticulum-derived COPII-coated vesicles, which function in ER to Golgi transport	Protein localized to COPII-coated vesicles, forms a complex with Erv41p; involved in the membrane fusion stage of transport	Protein involved in pre-rRNA processing, 18S rRNA synthesis, and snoRNA synthesis; component of the small subunit processome complex, which is required for processing of pre-18S rRNA	Protein required for mitochondrial translation; mutation is functionally complemented by a Bacillus subtilis ortholog	Mitochondrial ribosomal protein of the small subunit	Mitochondrial ribosomal protein of the large subunit, not essential for mitochondrial translation	Component of serine palmitoyltransferase, responsible along with Lcb2p for the first committed step in sphingolipid synthesis, which is the condensation of serine with palmitoyl-CoA to form 3-ketosphinganine	Hsp70 protein that interacts with Zuo1p (a DnaJ homolog) to form a ribosome-associated complex that binds the ribosome via the Zuo1p subunit; also involved in pleiotropic drug resistance via sequential activation of PDR1 and PDR5; binds ATP	Subunit of tRNA methyltransferase (MTase) complexes in combination with Trm9p and Trm11p; subunit of complex with Mtq2p that methylates Sup45p (eRF1) in the ternary complex eRF1-eRF3-GTP; deletion confers resistance to zymocin	Mitochondrial protein required for respiratory growth; mutant phenotype and genetic interactions suggest a role in delivering mt mRNAs to ribosomes; located on matrix face of the inner membrane and loosely associated with mitoribosomes	Alpha subunit of COPI vesicle coatomer complex, which surrounds transport vesicles in the early secretory pathway	Amidase, removes the amide group from N-terminal asparagine and glutamine residues to generate proteins with N-terminal aspartate and glutamate residues that are targets of ubiquitin-mediated degradation	Component (70 kDa) of the TOM (translocase of outer membrane) complex responsible for recognition and initial import steps for all mitochondrially directed proteins; acts as a receptor for incoming precursor proteins	Subunit of cleavage polyadenylation factor (CPF), interacts directly with poly(A) polymerase (Pap1p) to regulate its activity	Subunit of the Nup84p subcomplex of the nuclear pore complex (NPC), localizes to both sides of the NPC, required to establish a normal nucleocytoplasmic concentration gradient of the GTPase Gsp1p	Cytoplasmic inorganic pyrophosphatase (PPase), catalyzes the rapid exchange of oxygens from Pi with water, highly expressed and essential for viability, active-site residues show identity to those from E. coli PPase	Protein involved in homologous recombination in mitochondria and in transcription regulation in nucleus; binds to activation domains of acidic activators; required for recombination-dependent mtDNA partitioning	Nucleolar protein, component of the small subunit (SSU) processome containing the U3 snoRNA that is involved in processing of pre-18S rRNA	None	RNA polymerase III subunit C160, part of core enzyme; similar to bacterial beta-prime subunit	Protein required for transport of flavin adenine dinucleotide (FAD), a synthesis product of riboflavin, across the mitochondrial membrane	Protein required for transport of flavin adenine dinucleotide (FAD), a synthesis product of riboflavin, across the mitochondrial membrane	Subunit of holo-CPF, a multiprotein complex and functional homolog of mammalian CPSF, required for the cleavage and polyadenylation of mRNA and snoRNA 3' ends; involved in pre-tRNA processing; binds to the phosphorylated CTD of RNAPII	Mitochondrial intermembrane space protein that functions in mitochondrial copper ho